       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema has also been reported in overdose.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a typical starting dose.\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail patient or one with hepatic concerns.\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. For example, it could be part of a protocol I'm not aware of. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it now."
