      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A single 50 mg dose of amlodipine is in the range that causes serious toxicity in a 70 kg adult. Once-daily dosing would also make it worse, because amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours and the drug accumulates. I don't know of any indication that supports this dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily is the maximum, and 5 mg is a typical starting dose.\n- **Help with inadequate blood pressure control.** If 10 mg isn't enough, the usual next step is adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic. I can enter that order.\n- **Route an unusual protocol through pharmacy.** If this is part of a protocol I don't know about, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending first. The order can be entered once they've reviewed it.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
